 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t an objective “best”—the right choice depends on your type of injury, the lawyer’s experience with similar cases, and how well they communicate.\n\nFor an **injured person bringing a claim** (rather than an insurer or defendant), **Megan Burns or Emily L. Dahm at Mirador Law** are worth interviewing: the listings I found identify both as handling plaintiff-side personal injury, and report Super Lawyers selections from 2018–2026. **Paulo S. Kline Simon** is another Pleasanton-based plaintiff-side personal injury option listed by Super Lawyers.\n\nBefore hiring anyone, confirm their current California Bar status and ask:\n- How many cases like yours have they handled, and who will personally manage yours?\n- What is the contingency fee, and what case costs might you owe?\n- How often will they update you, and what happens if the case goes to trial?\n\nConsider speaking with two or three lawyers before deciding; many offer free initial consultations.",
